==Luo==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|en|ar}} {{m|ar|قلم|  pen}}

From {{der|ar|grc|κάλαμος||reed}}. {{w|Theodor Nöldeke|Nöldeke}} and {{w|Arthur Jeffery|Jeffery}} are convinced that it comes thence via {{bor|ar|gez|ቀለም|t={{l|en|reed}}}}, while {{w|Wolf Leslau|Leslau}} notes that {{m|gez|ቀለም|t={{l|en|reed}}}} could come from Arabic. But the meaning “reed” – referring to a plant – is not actually attested for the Arabic word, and given the peculiar semantics in Ge'ez where the word {{m|gez|ቀለም}} is mixed into the root of {{m|gez|ቀለመ|t=to {{l|en|color}}, to {{l|en|stain}}, to {{l|en|write}}}} and as well means “{{l|en|color}}”, “{{l|en|ink}}”, “{{l|en|inkstand}}”, as Leslau separates himself, a Ge'ez origin can explain why in Arabic the meaning is restricted to “pen” in the beginning compared with the {{cog|grc|κάλαμος}} meaning “reed cane” in general.

